<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Spot supplies very tight.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Spot supplies very tight.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis offers in U.S. cash soybean meal markets were steady to slightly lower on Thursday, but many brokers reported that they were out of meal for spot shipment.</p>
<p>&quot;We're out and that's pretty much going to be the case for the rest of November,&quot; said one river broker. &quot;And everybody seems to have covered their needs at least through the Thanksgiving holiday.&quot;</p>
<p>Brokers were still looking for a large National Oilseed Processors weekly crush figure. Estimates ranged from 29.5 to 30.6 million bushels.</p>
<p>Snow in Minnesota has slowed trade in some areas, but brokers there reported that demand in front of the Thanksgiving holiday remained robust.  </p>
